{"name":"Old Glory Red","hex":"#bf0a30","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"old","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mochi."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an object, concept, relationship, etc., having existed for a relatively long period of time.","Of a living being, having lived for most of the expected years."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old"},{"term":"glory","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Great beauty and splendor.","Honour, admiration, or distinction, accorded by common consent to a person or thing; high reputation; renown."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To exult with joy; to rejoice.","To boast; to be proud."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glory"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Old Glory","blocks":[{"text":"Old Glory is a nickname for the flag of the United States. The original \"Old Glory\" was a flag owned by the 19th-century American sea captain William Driver. He flew the flag during his career at sea and later brought it to Nashville, Tennessee, where he settled. Driver greatly prized the flag and ensured its safety from the Confederates, who attempted to seize the flag during the American Civil War. In 1922, Driver's daughter and niece claimed to own the original \"Old Glory\", which became part of the collection of the Smithsonian Institution, which remains at the National Museum of American History."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/76/Williamdriverflag.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Glory","wikidata":"Q7084096"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/69/Grave_maker_for_William_Driver.jpg/500px-Grave_maker_for_William_Driver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/69/Grave_maker_for_William_Driver.jpg/1280px-Grave_maker_for_William_Driver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/69/Grave_maker_for_William_Driver.jpg/500px-Grave_maker_for_William_Driver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Grave marker of sea captain William Driver, who coined the \"Old Glory\" nickname in reference to his own oceangoing flag.[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrave_maker_for_William_Driver.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Captain_William_Driver_Next_To_%22Old_Glory%22.